    "id": "p51-q21-response",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "21",
    "prompt": "True or False? Let $A$, $B$ and $C$ be sets in a universal set $U$.\n\n$A\\cup(B\\cap C)=(A\\cup B)\\cap(A\\cup C)$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "True.",
      "worked": "True. An element in $A$ belongs to both sides. An element outside $A$ belongs to either side exactly when it is in both $B$ and $C$. Thus both sides contain the same elements.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
